 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-11",
  "asof": "2026-09-14 10:23 UTC",
  "headline": "CPI came in line and the bond market called it a hike \u2014 Wednesday is now 86% priced",
  "standfirst": "August CPI rose 0.4% on the month and 3.4% on the year, both as expected, with core a tenth hot at +0.3%. Equities took it as relief and broke a four-day losing streak \u2014 the S&P rose 1.06% \u2014 while Treasury yields set fresh 52-week highs across the curve, the ten-year at 4.959%, and odds of a hike on Wednesday went to 85.6% from roughly 70%. The dovish condition this brief set on 4 September has failed outright: 3.4% against a 3.0% test, moving up rather than down. Oil eased for the first time in a week, WTI \u22123.35% to $99.05. Marks below are Thursday's, so Palantir's stop \u2014 0.75% away \u2014 is still unconfirmed. Heat 4.04R against 3.0R.",
  "themes": [],
  "ondeck": "The FOMC meets Tuesday and Wednesday and decides on 16 September with a hike 85.6% priced; the Bank of Japan meets this week with a hike 97% priced; triple witching is Friday 18 September. The next brief covers Monday's session.",
  "note": null
